natural_abilities:
  - name: "Supernatural P.S. and P.E."
    description: "Both attributes are supernatural; punch damage is read from the Supernatural P.S. table."
  - name: "Nightvision"
    description: "800 feet (244 m)."
  - name: "Keen Vision"
    description: "Excellent color vision. Whisker-like feelers around the mouth also let it sense things in darkness and on the sea floor."
  - name: "See the Invisible"
    description: "Including Astral Travelers, Entities and the essences of Alien Intelligences."
  - name: "Turn Invisible at Will"
    description: "At will."
  - name: "Bio-Regeneration"
    description: "1D4x10 M.D.C. per minute."
  - name: "Impervious to Cold"
    description: "Cold does no damage, not even magical mega-damage cold."
  - name: "Teleport Self"
    description: "50% +3% per level of experience, +20% if the destination is well known."
  - name: "Dimensional Teleport"
    description: "24% +4% per level of experience."
  - name: "Breathing"
    description: "Needs no air, and endures the pressure of the deep ocean or the vacuum of space without difficulty."
  - name: "Depth Tolerance"
    description: "Unlimited."
  - name: "Breath Weapon: Cold"
    description: "A blast of icy mist doing 3D6 M.D. of cold damage (5D6 M.D. from an adult), range 120 feet (36.6 m). Each blast counts as one melee attack."
  - name: "Metamorphosis"
    description: "Becomes an animal or humanoid of any kind, provided the shape walks on legs, is at least rabbit-sized and is no bigger than the dragon, for three hours per level of experience."
  - name: "Metamorphosis: Water"
    description: "Its body turns to water that is still alive and still the dragon. Out of the sea that means a puddle that flows under doors and through small openings, vents, grates, drains and water pipes, travelling at half its running speed, with NO attacks possible. Underwater it cannot be detected by any conventional means - sonar, nightvision, sound, heat or thermal sensing, even see the invisible, because it is not invisible but water inside water. In water form it is impervious to physical attacks and cannot attack by any means: it must turn physical to attack, even with psionics."
  - name: "Quick Turns and Stops"
    description: "Stops dead and turns completely around in tight spaces underwater."
  - name: "Sense Magnetic North"
    description: "The same as a dolphin."
  - name: "Chemoreceptors"
    description: "A highly developed sense of taste and smell. It tracks prey at 76% +2% per level of experience and identifies chemicals, toxins or specific creatures from a scent trail at 60% +2% per level. It can also judge the salt content or toxicity of water, and picks up blood in the water by taste the way a shark does."
  - name: "Natural Weapons"
    description: "Damage varies with Supernatural P.S. The claws are literally silver, deadly to supernatural beings vulnerable to that metal; punching with a claw adds 2D6 M.D. to punch damage, and a gore with the tusks at its mouth adds 3D6 M.D. Its bite is worth 5D6 M.D., and an adult''s 2D6 M.D. more. The prehensile tail whips for punch damage, and a power tail strike does double but counts as two melee actions. Ramming with all its weight at or near top swimming speed does 2D4x10 M.D. and counts as three melee actions. It may instead use magic, psionics or a weapon. Apart from the bite and the breath weapon, the book prints these once and does not give the hatchling smaller figures."
restrictions:
  - "Alignment: any. The species tends to Principled (35%), Scrupulous (30%), Unprincipled (10%) or Anarchist (10%)."
  - "Speed: 2D6+10 on land, where it crawls like a snake, but 6D6+30 swimming in or under water."
  - "Attacks per melee: four physical or psionic attacks per melee round, or two by magic, or any combination of them."
  - "The +1 on Perception Rolls becomes +2 on anything involving water."
  - "+1 on all saving throws other than Horror Factor (which is +3)."
  - "Prowl is +10% in water only."
  - "VULNERABILITIES: it dislikes fire, heat and fire attacks: mega-damage plasma and magic fire inflict double damage."
  - "MAGIC: born with a full understanding of magic but knows NO spells at level one. It can learn magic, and can use Techno-Wizard, Biomancy and other magical weapons and devices. Under the Rifts Ultimate Edition hatchling rules the book points to (p.158), spells are learned by the usual means from second level - by third level the hatchling has 2D4+2 spells from levels 1-3, another 2D4+2 by fifth level from levels 3-8, and 3 new spells per level thereafter up to its own level. Two spells may be cast per melee round, and it gains +1 to spell strength at level nine. Those counts are dice-valued, which a spell schedule cannot hold, so they are recorded here."
  - "PSIONICS: a Master Psychic. Empathy, Meditation and Mind Block, plus five Hydro-Psionic abilities of choice (the fifteen listed under the Spouter O.C.C., p.81). One new Hydro-Psionic ability at each new level of experience, the Hydrokinesis Super-Psionic power at level 4 and P.P.E. Shield at level 8."
  - "On S.D.C. worlds a hatchling has 180 Hit Points, 2D6x10+25 S.D.C. and a Natural A.R. of 10 in place of its M.D.C."
  - "Size: 36-50 feet (10.9 to 15.2 m) long and 12-20 tons. It has no hind legs in dragon form. The book prints no separate hatchling size."
  - "Hydros Dragons are nobody''s war steed or pet, but have been known to let heroes ride behind the shoulders or on the neck."
  - "From Rifts Ultimate Edition p.158, Magic Knowledge: without being taught it can work any Techno-Wizard device, recognise and use other magic weapons, read magic and use scrolls, and it recognises magic circles and enchantment at 40% +3% per level of experience. It senses ley lines and nexus points within 20 miles (32 km), and other dragons - even ones disguised by metamorphosis - on sight out to 4000 feet (1219 m). The sensing gives nearness and general direction, never an exact spot."
  - "From Rifts Ultimate Edition p.158, Weapons and Equipment: it can use any kind of weapon, and wears little clothing or mega-damage armor except as a disguise in humanoid form. It mostly counts on what it was born with, its magic and its psionics."
  - "From the Rifts Ultimate Edition hatchling rules (p.156-159) the book defers to: a hatchling behaves like a child of four to seven and must settle on a definitive alignment at level three; it does not need to eat or drink; it can never take cybernetics or bionics, which its bio-regeneration pushes back out; and under 100 years old it cares little for wealth, though it is always drawn to magic items."
side_effects: "ADULT HYDROS DRAGON (not playable; the class stores the hatchling). Attributes I.Q. 2D6+12, M.E. 2D6+15, M.A. 2D6+12, P.S. 2D6+28, P.P. 2D6+10, P.E. 3D6+10, P.B. 4D6+6, Spd 1D6+18 on land (about 15 mph/24 km) and 1D6x10+90 swimming (75-80 mph), without tiring. M.D.C. 1D6x1,000+800, +1D6x1,000 for an ancient (S.D.C. worlds: 4D6x10+100 Hit Points, 3D6x100+200 S.D.C., Natural A.R. 14). Horror Factor 14. P.P.E. 1D6x100+180. I.S.P. 3D6x10 + M.E., +10 per level; all Hydro-Psionic abilities plus Group Mind Block, Hydrokinesis, Mind Bolt and P.P.E. Shield. Seven physical or psionic attacks per melee round, or four by magic. +2 on Perception Rolls (+5 involving water), +2 initiative, +3 strike and parry, +1 dodge (+4 automatic dodge underwater), +5 pull punch, +4 roll with impact, +6 vs Horror Factor, +2 on all other saves. Breath 5D6 M.D.; bite 5D6 M.D. +2D6 M.D. Magic: one of Ocean Magic (40%), Wizard/Spell Invocations as a Ley Line Walker (30%) or Whale Songs (30%), about 3D6+16 spells; never Warlock, Shifter or Necromancy. Life span 1D6x1,000+2,000 years, some reaching 9,000. NPC level: 2D4 for adults, 1D4 for hatchlings. Also called the Water Dragon or Aqua Dragon. It fights the undead and supernatural evil, and counts as natural enemies the Lord of the Deep, the Milu, vampires and any dragon gone bad. It fears fire and distrusts fire-breathers and fire magic."
extraction_notes: |
  Read from Rifts World Book 32: Lemuria printed 215-216 (cache p216-p217;
  printed 214 is full-page art). Every figure was read off renders of printed
  215 (both columns) and the left column of printed 216, where the entry ends;
  the right column of 216 is the Octo Dragon. The text layer scrambles the
  paragraph order on 216, so the hatchling lines were paired with their
  headings on the render: the cache''s "level4" is level 4.

  Section heading: "Sea Dragons" (printed 208). A race, so no men_of_arms
  line is needed: the class states mdc_base.

  WHAT THE BOOK DEFERS TO RIFTS ULTIMATE EDITION, AND WHAT WAS REUSED.
  The entry says "Hatchling player characters start at level one" and twice
  sends the reader to Rifts Ultimate Edition p.156 for playing a dragon
  hatchling. Taken from the published dragon-hatchling-flame-wind class, not
  from this book:
  1. xp_table - the Rifts Ultimate Edition dragon ladder, copied from
     dragon-hatchling-flame-wind. This entry prints no ladder; the Leviathan
     in the same section (printed 209-210) says to use the Dragon Experience
     Table. Rifts Ultimate Edition''s Experience Tables (printed 295) head
     this ladder "Dragon Hatchling & Adult Dragon", and its hatchling
     section (printed 158) says to use the Dragon R.C.C. for level
     advancement.
  2. The spell-learning progression in the MAGIC restriction, and the last
     restriction line (alignment at level three, no need to eat, no
     cybernetics, money). This book prints only "know no spells at Level
     One ... can learn magic and use Techno-Wizard, Biomancy and other magical
     weapons and devices".
  3. The Magic Knowledge and Weapons and Equipment restriction lines, and
     "two spells per melee round, +1 to spell strength at level nine" in the
     MAGIC line. Rifts Ultimate Edition printed 158 prints all three in its
     general Dragon Hatchling section, as rules for every hatchling (the
     cache prints the spell strength figure as "+f"; it is +1).
  NOT reused: Rifts Ultimate Edition''s skill scheme (instinctive skills at
  98%, Secondary Skills, Special Areas of Interest). This entry prints its own
  "R.C.C. Skills (Hatchling)" list, which is what is stored.

  WHAT THE BOOK PRINTS AND WHAT WAS STORED.
  1. Skills: 15 named skills with a printed bonus; each base is the catalog
     base plus that bonus. "Pilot: Sail Boats" is held as Boat: Sail Type,
     "Pilot: Water Scooters" as Water Scooters, "Pilot: Water Skiing and
     Surfing" as Water Skiing & Surfing, "Underwater Navigation" as
     Navigation: Underwater, "Lore: Demon and Monster" as Lore: Demons &
     Monsters, "Literate in Dragonese/Elven" as Literacy: Dragonese/Elven.
  2. "Prowl (+10% in water only)" is conditional: Prowl is stored at the
     catalog''s 25% and the +10% is prose.
  3. "A total of four skill selections from ... Aquatic, Communication,
     Domestic, Science, Technical and Wilderness" is stored as a four-pick
     choice group in occ_skills with bonus 0. The catalog has no Aquatic
     category: the book''s Aquatic Skills list (printed 54) is spread over
     Technical, Wilderness, Science, Horsemanship, Medical and Pilot Related,
     so Horsemanship and Medical are named with `only` lists holding the
     Aquatic skills filed there. Left out: Horsemanship: Serpent Hunter (the Serpent
     Hunter''s own) and Navigation: Underwater (Pilot Related; already an
     R.C.C. skill here). A single { name: "Aquatic", only: [...] } entry was
     tested and is refused by categoryAllows: a cross-category `only` is
     admitted only when the group also lists the skill''s real category.
  4. "Magically understands and speaks all languages at 90%" is stored as
     Language: All (magical) at 90 with no per-level gain.
  5. Attacks: "Four physical or psionic attacks, or two by magic" is stored as
     attacks_base 4.
  6. "+1 on all other saving throws" is stored as +1 on each of the fourteen
     other d20 saves the sheet draws (the percentile coma/death save is left
     alone), following dragon-hatchling-asama-tatsu, and is also kept as a
     restriction line.
  7. Perception +1 is stored; "+2 to anything involving water" is prose.
  8. Horror Factor 10 is stored in horror_factor.
  9. The S.D.C.-world figures (180 Hit Points, 2D6x10+25 S.D.C.) are stored in
     hit_points_base and sdc_base as the flame-wind model does; Natural A.R.
     10 is prose.
  10. Psionics: "Five Hydro-Psionic abilities of choice (see the Spouter
      O.C.C. for these powers), +1 new Hydro-Psionic ability for each new
      level" is read as the fifteen under "Alphabetical Listing of
      Hydro-Psionics" on printed 81, NOT the six under "Hydro-Super-Psionics".
      The list is named in powers_from and again on every schedule entry,
      because the catalog files these under the shared category Special and a
      schedule replaces a flat per-level count. Printed 82 heads the powers
      "Hydro-Psionics exclusive to the Spouter"; this entry grants them anyway.
      Hydrokinesis at level 4 and P.P.E. Shield at level 8 are one-name
      schedule entries.
  11. Spd stores the land figure (2D6+10); swimming Spd 6D6+30 is prose.
  12. Adult and ancient figures are prose only (side_effects). Bite: "5D6
      M.D. (+2D6 M.D. from adults)" - the hatchling''s is 5D6. Cold breath 3D6
      M.D., 5D6 from adults.

  BOOK SLIPS.
  - Printed 216: the Chemoreceptors paragraph calls it the "Hydro Dragon".
  - Printed 215: water form travels at "half its running speed"; the
    hatchling''s land Spd is printed as crawling, 2D6+10. Recorded as printed.
  - Printed 215-216: apart from the bite and the breath weapon, Mega-Damage,
    the size and the natural abilities do not separate adult from hatchling.
    Stored once, as printed.
---

## Lore

A silver-blue dragon with a silver belly, a body that tapers into a snake''s
tail where the hind legs would be, webbed forelimbs, and claws of actual
silver. People who see one in the water often take it for a sea serpent. It is
as happy ashore as at sea, deserts aside, and seeks out reefs, lagoons,
waterfalls, forests and ice.

The Hydros is the gentle one among the sea dragons: fond of music and art,
moved by beauty, distressed by cruelty, and friendly with Lemurians, Merans,
dolphins and whales. That makes the change startling when it does fight,
because it fights the undead and the demonic with no restraint at all.

A hatchling is a strong swimmer and a Master Psychic whose powers work through
water. Its signature trick is to turn into water outright: a puddle that pours
through a keyhole on land, and something that simply cannot be found once it
is in the sea.

## GM Notes

Water form is a scouting and escape power, not a combat one: nothing physical
can hurt it and it can hurt nothing, psionics included, until it turns solid
again. The book does not say what magic or energy attacks do to it in that
form.

Fire is the lever against it. Mega-damage plasma and magical fire do double
damage, and the dragon knows it.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'dragon-hatchling-hydros');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
